    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115-a1">

                <pb facs="0212" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v5/pg182"/>

                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1857-11-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#small-caps">November</hi> 9,
                        1857</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Canal de Haro, or Arro, is undoubtedly the navigable channel which, at its
                    position, separates <hi rendition="#italic">Vancouver’s Island</hi> from the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">continent,</hi> and therefore, while other channels
                    exist more adjacent to the continent, cannot be the channel which “separates the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">continent</hi> from <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vancouver’s Island</hi>.”</p>
            </div>
        </body>
